        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(signal): add guided setup wizard",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a problem where Signal setup could require users to manually assemble a working Signal transport before OpenClaw could receive messages. The setup wizard now offers a Docker-backed `signal-cli-rest-api` path, keeps existing Signal server setup available, and records the transport mode so status, probe, send, and receive flows use the right API shape.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe change keeps Signal-specific setup behavior inside the Signal plugin while adding the narrow core setup-wizard and SDK seams needed for plugin-owned setup. It adds container/native/auto transport handling, account-scoped `apiMode`, Docker QR/linking setup, setup rollback behavior, status/probe reporting, and docs for the supported config.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can set up Signal from the setup wizard with either a local Docker helper or an existing Signal server, then see accurate channel status without hand-editing config. Operators also get clearer install/setup failure messages and config that preserves per-account transport mode for future sends, receives, and probes.\n\n## Evidence\n\nBehavioral proof:\n\n- Signal setup wizard E2E passed in a scratch setup pane using a scratch config under `/tmp/openclaw-signal-real-tui`; no real user config was touched and no manual Signal messages were sent.\n- Scratch gateway probe proof reached the Signal channel through the scratch config and gateway path after the setup flow wrote `channels.signal` with `httpUrl` and container `apiMode`.\n- Existing Signal server setup and Docker setup are both covered by focused setup-core tests, including QR/link handling, account linking validation, setup cancellation rollback, and transport classification.\n- Account-scoped `apiMode` routing is covered for sends, typing, read receipts, reactions, probe/check, and receive streaming.\n\nReviewer-checkable validation:\n\n- Native review against `origin/main` completed with zero actionable findings on the final target.\n- Independent cold review of `origin/main...HEAD` completed with zero actionable findings.\n- `OPENCLAW_VITEST_MAX_WORKERS=1 node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/signal/src/core.test.ts -t \"container|Docker|existing Signal server|apiMode|setup status|endpoint-only|Signal setup choice\"` passed: 1 file, 27 tests, 61 skipped.\n- `OPENCLAW_VITEST_MAX_WORKERS=1 node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/signal/src/client-adapter.test.ts extensions/signal/src/send.test.ts extensions/signal/src/send-reactions.test.ts extensions/signal/src/config-schema.test.ts extensions/signal/setup-entry.test.ts src/channels/plugins/setup-helpers.test.ts src/flows/channel-setup.test.ts src/commands/channels.surfaces-signal-runtime-errors-channels-status-output.test.ts` passed: 8 files across 4 shards, 119 tests.\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD` passed.\n- `pnpm docs:list` completed; the relevant Signal channel docs are updated.\n\nNo browser screenshot is included because this PR changes CLI/setup, plugin runtime, config, and docs behavior rather than a browser-rendered UI surface.\n",
